# Factory runtime/generated artifacts are local by default (ACT-CLINEMM-FORK-BASELINE01).
# NOTE: Git cannot re-include a file when its parent directory itself is excluded,
# so the .factory directory must remain traversable and only its contents ignored.
# The canonical epic board is the exception and is durably tracked below.
# See ACT-CLINEMM-FACTORY-BOARD-DURABILITY-AND-FACTORIZE-INTAKE01.
/.factory/*
!/.factory/epic-board.md
# ACT-CLINEMM-FACTORY-EPIC-BOARD-SHARDING01: per-epic detail files under
# .factory/epics/ are durable, linkable substrate of the board architecture.
# See docs/factory-migrations/ACT-CLINEMM-FACTORY-EPIC-BOARD-SHARDING01-manifest.md.
!/.factory/epics/
# ACT-CLINEMM-TOOL-EXECUTION-SEMANTICS-IMPLEMENTATION01 (TES-IMPL-01): the
# implementation ACT contract is referenced from durable board and epic
# files, so the ACT itself MUST be durable (otherwise the canonical link
# would be broken on a fresh clone). Parked / waiting-for-evidence ACTs
# stay local — they have no durable binding contract yet.
#
# Policy: DEFAULT-DENY + WHITELIST. The `.factory/acts/` directory
# itself is re-included so git can recurse, but every file *under* it
# is ignored unless explicitly whitelisted below. This is forward-safe:
# any new file dropped under `.factory/acts/` (a future debug dump, a
# scratch ACT, a captured secret-bearing log) is local-by-default
# without needing to update this gitignore first. The policy contract
# is the gitignore rule itself, not a maintained inventory of known
# local-only filenames.
!/.factory/acts/
/.factory/acts/*
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-TOOL-EXECUTION-SEMANTICS-IMPLEMENTATION01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-TERMINAL-REPORT-COMPLETION-FRAMING01-CORRECTION01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-PTAD-ENV-OPTIN01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-COMPLETION-PROTOCOL-LIVENESS02.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-YOLO-COMPLETION-AUTHORITY-CONTRACT01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-YOLO-COMPLETION-AUTHORITY-IMPLEMENTATION01.md
# ACT-CLINEMM-EDITOR-TOOL-APPROVAL-FRICTION-RECON01: launched 2026-08-27.
# Status NEXT / HIGH (approval-protection lane); recon §2 PASS_RECON_SEAM_MAPPED
# at HEAD f8dca1fda / TREE 6f2e01b56; live specimen §3 deferred behind the
# IMPLEMENTATION01 predecessor. The epic ledger at
# .factory/epics/approval-protection.md row 19 binds to the ACT file AND to
# the evidence file .factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-EDITOR-TOOL-APPROVAL-FRICTION-RECON01/source-seam-map.md,
# so both must be durably tracked for the canonical link to survive a
# fresh clone.
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-EDITOR-TOOL-APPROVAL-FRICTION-RECON01.md
# ACT-CLINEMM-APPROVAL-SPECIMEN-CAPTURE-TOOL01-CORRECTION01: bounded
# correction ACT authored 2026-08-27 against the editor-tool recon
# ACT's evidence-acquisition toolchain (capture-approval-specimen.py).
# Status OPEN / HIGH. The correction ACT binds to the editor-tool
# recon ACT (which it corrects) and to the binding record
# .factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-EDITOR-TOOL-APPROVAL-FRICTION-RECON01/captures/specimen-20260827-command-approval01.json,
# so the ACT file AND the captures/ binding record must both be
# durably tracked for the canonical link to survive a fresh clone.
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-APPROVAL-SPECIMEN-CAPTURE-TOOL01-CORRECTION01.md
# Same durable-binding reason as the ACT file above.
# Mirror the .factory/acts/ default-deny + whitelist pattern:
#   1. re-include the .factory/evidence/ directory so git can recurse,
#   2. deny everything under it by default,
#   3. whitelist the directory contents that have a durable-binding
#      contract with an epic ledger / ACT file.
!/.factory/evidence/
/.factory/evidence/*
!/.factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-EDITOR-TOOL-APPROVAL-FRICTION-RECON01/
# ACT-CLINEMM-APPROVAL-SPECIMEN-CAPTURE-TOOL01-CORRECTION01 evidence
# (hermetic-fixture/happy-path-matrix.json + negative-matrix.json).
# Same durable-binding reason as the ACT file: the matrices prove
# the corrected collector's P0.2 / P0.3 / P1 invariants end-to-end.
!/.factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-APPROVAL-SPECIMEN-CAPTURE-TOOL01-CORRECTION01/
# ACT-CLINEMM-TASK-COST-TRUTH-RECON01: backlog recon ACT authored
# 2026-08-27. Status OPEN / HIGH (cost provenance lane). Recon §2
# PASS_RECON_SURFACE_MAPPED at the commit of authorship; §3 live
# matrix frozen later. The epic ledger at
# .factory/epics/product-config-branding.md will bind to this ACT
# file AND to the evidence directory
# .factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-TASK-COST-TRUTH-RECON01/, so both
# must be durably tracked for the canonical link to survive a fresh
# clone.
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-TASK-COST-TRUTH-RECON01.md
!/.factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-TASK-COST-TRUTH-RECON01/
# ACT-CLINEMM-UPSTREAM-SETTINGS-SURFACE-PARITY-RECON01: backlog
# recon ACT authored 2026-08-27. Status OPEN / MED-HIGH (settings
# webview inventory lane). Recon §2 PASS_RECON_SURFACE_MAPPED at
# the commit of authorship; §3 inventory frozen later. Same
# durable-binding reason as the cost-truth ACT above: the owning
# epic (decided by §11 of the ACT, not pre-baked) and the evidence
# directory must both survive a fresh clone.
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-UPSTREAM-SETTINGS-SURFACE-PARITY-RECON01.md
!/.factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-UPSTREAM-SETTINGS-SURFACE-PARITY-RECON01/
# ACT-CLINEMM-RUNTIME-TASK-PROGRESSION-RECON01: recon ACT
# LAUNCH_HEAD = cf40c2b8b07520f9ddc2d798c6dfbb9830df9dea (the commit that
# introduced this ACT; canonical binding per 5b0fbd611 "docs(factory): bind
# runtime-progression launch identity"). ENTRY_HEAD = a2417ef19 (pre-ACT
# subject; see entry-freeze.txt). Promoted from OPEN / WAITING_FOR_LIVE_EVIDENCE
# to OPEN / LIVE_RUNNING_STATE_BOUND / AWAITING_TERMINAL_DISCRIMINATOR at
# TRIAGE_BIND 2026-08-28 on TRIAGE_HEAD = 15f2adaf6. The live-failure.json,
# red-result.txt, source-seam-map.md and upstream-comparison.md files now
# carry the awaited live RUNNING-state specimen (background-command specimen
# cmd_mtcjhkhygpteq8v9) and the seam map for TOOL_RESULT_TERMINAL_SEAM /
# TASK_OWNER_SEAM against current source. The epic ledger at
# .factory/epics/runtime-task-progression.md row 58 binds to the ACT file
# AND to the evidence directory, so both must be durably tracked for the
# canonical link to survive a fresh clone. The contract remains UNDEFINED
# (HOST_DEFERRED_FOREGROUND_OWNERSHIP_CONTRACT) and OWNED/AWAITED-vs-DETACHED
# is recorded as a PRODUCT_CONTRACT_CANDIDATE only — no implementation work
# is authorized by this whitelisting. Note: the bound specimen only proves
# the RUNNING-state half of the lifecycle; the post-terminal chronology
# (terminal status / exit, onBackgroundStateChange(false, jobId), runtime
# phase after, continuation emitted?, UI still Waiting?) is UNOBSERVED and
# must be captured before LIVE_FAILURE_BOUND can be promoted to PASS.
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-RUNTIME-TASK-PROGRESSION-RECON01.md
!/.factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-RUNTIME-TASK-PROGRESSION-RECON01/


# Same principle for nested Factory state under apps/vscode (ACT-CLINEMM-DOGFOOD-BUILD-EVIDENCE-IGNORE01).
# apps/vscode/.factory/evidence/ holds generated local evidence from dogfood / seatbelt
# qualification runs and must NOT block exact-head VSIX packaging (build-dogfood-vsix.py
# runs `git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all` and HALTs on any ?? entry).
# The repo-root /  .factory/* rule above only matches paths whose first component
# is `.factory/`; Git's anchoring in /.factory/* means `apps/vscode/.factory/...`
# is NOT covered by it, so this symmetric rule is required.
apps/vscode/.factory/evidence/

# Factory staging/backup siblings (µC-3 round 6 atomic publish)
.factory-staging-*
.factory-backup-*

# Factory staging/backup siblings (µC-3 round 7 atomic publish)
.factory-leamas-staging-*

# Python build artifacts (ACT-CLINEMM-REPRODUCIBLE-DOGFOOD-VSIX01)
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
